layout: base.njk
permalink: /act/
title: Take Action
description: What we're asking for, and how to help stop the data center at 4405 Route 1 in South Brunswick, NJ.
---
{% set c = campaigns["south-brunswick"] %}
<section class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">South Brunswick data center</p>
    <h1>Take action</h1>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="wrap section">
  <h2>Ways to help</h2>
  <ol class="steps-big">
    <li id="governor">
      <div><strong>Ask Governor Sherrill to pause new data centers</strong><br>Things to raise, in your own words:
        <ul class="talk">
          <li><strong>Pause new approvals</strong> until New Jersey has data center rules that protect the people living next to them.</li>
          <li><strong>Your plan covers costs, not pollution.</strong> Your data center plan addresses electricity costs, reporting, local agreements, and labor. None of it covers diesel generators next to homes. <a class="cite" href="https://newjerseymonitor.com/2026/05/27/governor-data-center-construction-limits/" rel="noopener">[NJ Monitor]</a></li>
          <li><strong>Close the loophole.</strong> Health tests should count emergency use, and when the worst case fails, require cleaner backup or pollution controls. <a class="cite" href="/south-brunswick/#testing-only">[details]</a></li>
          <li><strong>Your law could mean more diesel.</strong> The Data Center Fair Share law "requires data centers to cut back before residential ratepayers are impacted." Unless NJDEP restricts it, one way to cut back is to switch on diesel generators, and grid emergencies tend to come in heat waves. <a class="cite" href="https://www.nj.gov/governor/news/2026/20260707a.shtml" rel="noopener">[Governor's office]</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <a class="btn primary" href="{{ write.governor.form_url }}" rel="noopener">Contact</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div><strong>Write your state legislators</strong><br>We'll help you start, in your own words.</div>
      <a class="btn primary" href="/write/">Write</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div><strong>Join us</strong><br>Updates, meetings, and discussion.</div>
      <span class="joinlinks">{% for s in site.social %}<a class="btn small" href="{{ s.url }}" rel="noopener">{{ s.name }}</a> {% endfor %}<a class="btn small" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">Email</a></span>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="wrap section">
  <h2>More ways to help</h2>
  <ul class="morehelp">
    {% for a in c.actions %}
    <li{% if a.until %} data-until="{{ a.until }}"{% endif %}>
      <strong>{{ a.title }}.</strong> {{ a.text | mdInline | safe }}
      <a href="{{ a.url }}" rel="noopener">{{ a.button }} →</a>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="wrap section" id="demands">
  <h2>What we're asking for</h2>
  <ol class="demands">
    {% for d in c.demands %}
    <li><strong>{{ d.title }}</strong> {{ d.text | mdInline | safe }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
  <p class="muted small">Why these? See <a href="/south-brunswick/">the facts and sources</a>.</p>
</section>
